( F4 T6a / BACKLOG C56: a word longer than the 100-character parser
  buffer inside a comment, as the URL in line 2 of the Professional
  ground19_water_under_dam. The old GNU read it with an unbounded
  cin >> str into char str[100] and wrote past the buffer [ASan stack
  overflow; the results were right by layout luck]. Now the word is
  read in pieces of at most 99 characters and the comment is skipped
  as before: rc 0 and the target below.
  https://example.org/a/very/long/path/that/goes/on/and/on/well/past/the/hundred/character/limit/of/the/tochnog/parser/buffer/index.html
  Also a word of exactly 99 characters, the longest one that fits:
  abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzabcdefghijklmnopqrstu )
